{
  "title": "Namaz for more Sustenance",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is reported that a man came to the Holy Prophet (s) and said, \"I have many dependants and I am suffering too much because of debts. Therefore, instruct me a supplication by which Almighty Allah will provide me sustenance so that I can settle my debts and cover the needs of my dependants.\" The Holy Prophet (s) taught him to do the following: perform the ritual ablution very accurately, then offer a two-unit prayer with accurate genuflection (ruku') and prostration. Upon accomplishment, say the following supplication:\nيَا مَاجِدُ يَا وَاحِدُ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nYAA MAAJIDU YAA WAAHIDU YAA KAREEM\nO Majestic, O One, O Generous,\nاَتَوَجَّهُ اِلَيْكَ بِمُحَمَّدٍ نَبِيِّكَ نَبِىِّ الرَّحْمَةِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nATAWAJJAHU ILAYKA BI-MUHAMMADIN NABIYYIKA NABIYYIR RAHMATI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nI turn towards You through Muhammad, Your Prophet, the Prophet of mercy — Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household —\nيَا مُحَمَّدُ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nYAA MUHAMMADU YAA RASOOLALLAAH\nO Muhammad, O Messenger of Allah,\nاِنِّىْ اَتَوَجَّهُ بِكَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكَ وَرَبِّ كُلِّ شَيْئٍ\nINNEE ATAWAJJAHU BIKA ILALLAAHI RABBEE WA RABBIKA WA RABBI KULLI SHAY-IN\nverily I turn through you towards Allah, my Lord and your Lord and the Lord of all things,\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ اَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ\nWA AS-ALUKAL LAAHUMMA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIH\nand I ask You, O Allah, to send blessings upon Muhammad and the people of his household,\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ نَفْحَةً كَرِيْمَةً مِنْ نَفَحَاتِكَ وَفَتْحًا يَّسِيْرًا وَرِزْقًا وَاسِعًا\nWA AS-ALUKA NAFHATAN KAREEMATAM MIN NAFAHAATIKA WA FATHAN YASEERAN WA RIZQAN WAASI'AA\nand I ask You for a generous waft from among Your gracious wafts, an easy triumph, and an abundant sustenance\nاَلُمُّ بِهٖ شَعَثِىْ وَاَقْضِىْ بِهٖ دَيْنِىْ وَاَسْتَعِيْنُ بِهٖ عَلٰى عِيَالِىْ\nALUMMU BIHI SHA'ATHEE WA AQDEE BIHI DAYNEE WA ASTA'EENU BIHI A'LAA A'YAALEE\nwith which I may gather my scattered affairs, settle my debt, and seek help for the sake of my dependants."
}
